---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  activePage="about"
  title="About — João Jacinto"
  description="I design products that make things genuinely easier for the people who use them. Senior Product Designer based in Aveiro, Portugal."
  showCta={true}
>

  <div class="about-wrap">
    <div class="marquee about-marquee">
      <div class="marquee-track">
        <span>ABOUT ME</span><span>·</span><span>MY JOURNEY</span><span>·</span><span>HOW I WORK</span><span>·</span>
        <span>ABOUT ME</span><span>·</span><span>MY JOURNEY</span><span>·</span><span>HOW I WORK</span><span>·</span>
        <span>ABOUT ME</span><span>·</span><span>MY JOURNEY</span><span>·</span><span>HOW I WORK</span><span>·</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container">

      <section class="why-grid reveal">
        <div>
          <h2>I turn tangled problems into products people don't have to think about.</h2>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>I design for the moments where complexity is non-negotiable — products built on dense rule sets, layered permissions, or workflows that have to hold up under real operational weight. My approach is to systems-think first and design second: map the relationships, expose the logic, then strip away everything that isn't load-bearing.</p>
          <p>None of that works without staying close to the people using the product — learning from them, sitting with their feedback, and letting it shape the next decision. The goal is always the same: the person using the product should feel like the hard part was solved before they arrived. I work async by default, write things down, and share context early so the rest of the team isn't left chasing it.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="section-divider">

      <section class="about-me">
        <div class="about-grid">
          <div class="about-col reveal reveal-d1">
            <h3>Principles</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Make the invisible visible</li>
              <li>Cut what isn't load-bearing</li>
              <li>Stay close to the people using it</li>
              <li>Optimise for the next designer</li>
              <li>Strong opinions, written down</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="about-col reveal reveal-d2">
            <h3>Passions</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Music production, drums</li>
              <li>Building with AI</li>
              <li>RPGs and VR racing</li>
              <li>Premier league football</li>
              <li>3D printing</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="about-col reveal reveal-d3">
            <h3>Currently</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Building: <a href="https://www.anchorage.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Anchorage Digital</a></li>
              <li>Shipping: <a href="/">joaojacinto.com</a></li>
              <li>Listening: <a href="https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_mT0JOV9xVWCyrOWBjjfpjAF-0LfyxGVW8" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Vulfmon</a>, <a href="https://music.youtube.com/watch?v=I8NzXaIQY54" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Oli Howe</a></li>
              <li>Producing: <a href="https://music.youtube.com/watch?v=80hpbDstlhc&list=OLAK5uy_mex7K9FoXhQBxg8yKviL81Avmz9Xfh4WI" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Boreal Haze</a></li>
              <li>Reading: <a href="https://www.amazon.es/dp/1260474186?ref=ppx_yo2ov_dt_b_fed_asin_title" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Crucial Conversations</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="section-divider">

      <h2 class="stack-title reveal">My journey</h2>

      <div class="timeline">
      <section class="journey">
        <div class="journey-row reveal">
          <div class="journey-year">2024–now</div>
          <div>
            <div class="journey-title">
              <span class="journey-role">Member of Product Design Team (Senior IC)</span>
              <a class="journey-co" data-umami-event="about-company" data-umami-event-co="anchorage" href="https://www.anchorage.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">at Anchorage Digital</a>
            </div>
            <p class="journey-desc">Crypto/web3 infrastructure for institutional clients — Core Experience</p>
            <ul class="journey-achievements">
              <li class="journey-achievement">Redesigned the policies and permissions system — collapsed a 40-step admin flow into a single configuration step</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="journey-row reveal">
          <div class="journey-year">2022–2024</div>
          <div>
            <div class="journey-title">
              <span class="journey-role">Senior → Staff Product Designer</span>
              <a class="journey-co" data-umami-event="about-company" data-umami-event-co="streamyard" href="https://streamyard.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">at StreamYard</a>
            </div>
            <p class="journey-desc">Live streaming SaaS. Webinars product UX, research ops, and the design system.</p>
            <ul class="journey-achievements">
              <li class="journey-achievement">Tripled weekly webinar volume after shipping the customisation feature</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="journey-row reveal">
          <div class="journey-year">2021–2022</div>
          <div>
            <div class="journey-title">
              <span class="journey-role">Senior Product Designer</span>
              <a class="journey-co" data-umami-event="about-company" data-umami-event-co="talkdesk" href="https://www.talkdesk.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">at Talkdesk</a>
            </div>
            <p class="journey-desc">AI trainer for customer support — pre-LLM era.</p>
            <ul class="journey-achievements">
              <li class="journey-achievement">Redesigned the human-in-the-loop labeling tool that CX teams used to train conversational AI models — pre-LLM era</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="journey-row reveal">
          <div class="journey-year">2017–2021</div>
          <div>
            <div class="journey-title">
              <span class="journey-role">Product Designer</span>
              <a class="journey-co" data-umami-event="about-company" data-umami-event-co="namecheap" href="https://www.namecheap.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">at Namecheap</a>
            </div>
            <p class="journey-desc">Domains & hosting. Internal support tooling, iterating with 200+ agents daily.</p>
            <ul class="journey-achievements">
              <li class="journey-achievement">Hit 97.4% positive feedback within 4 months of launching the new chat &amp; support experience</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="journey-row reveal">
          <div class="journey-year">2015–2017</div>
          <div>
            <div class="journey-title">
              <span class="journey-role">UX/UI Designer</span>
              <a class="journey-co" data-umami-event="about-company" data-umami-event-co="beubi" href="https://github.com/beubi" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">at Be.Ubi</a>
            </div>
            <p class="journey-desc">3D printing software, plus a land registry system for a Portuguese municipality.</p>
            <ul class="journey-achievements">
              <li class="journey-achievement">Rebuilt the 3D printing software after embedding with the team and running client interviews</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="influences">
        <span class="eyebrow reveal">Roots &amp; Influences</span>
        <div class="influences-layout reveal reveal-d1">

          <div class="influences-narrative">
            <p>The line between design and engineering has always been a tool for me, not a fence.</p>
            <p>I was doing digital branding for friends at 13 — logos, profile graphics, whatever they needed — before I'd even thought of it as design. By 15 I was shipping front-end code: themes for Hi5 and MySpace, some pulling 50,000+ concurrent users. That loop of making something, watching people use it, and learning from what breaks set the pattern early.</p>
            <p>IT engineering taught me how products work; multimedia design was where I learned how they communicate. I pivoted because the second half was the one I couldn't stop thinking about — but I've kept both halves active. A decade across enterprise SaaS, crypto, live streaming, and AI tooling later, the engineering half still shapes how I design: I scope what's buildable, talk tradeoffs in engineers' language, and ship the real interaction when a mock can't carry the argument. With AI in the loop, that fluency matters more, not less — prompting a model to build something is still an engineering conversation, just at a higher level.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="influences-right" style="display:none">
            <div class="influences-block">
              <h3>Resources I learn from</h3>
