        </div>
      </section>
      </div>

      <hr class="section-divider">

      <section class="how-i-work" aria-labelledby="how-i-work-title">
        <h2 id="how-i-work-title" class="stack-title reveal">How I work</h2>

        <div class="how-i-work-grid">
          <div class="how-i-work-body">
          <p class="reveal">I've spent 10+ years shipping product, and the through-line isn't a tool — it's a habit: find the smallest version of the real problem, then build the smallest version of a real answer. Everything below is in service of that.</p>

          <p class="reveal">I start in conversation, not Figma. Most design mistakes I've watched ship started with someone opening a blank canvas before the problem was understood. So I spend more time than feels comfortable in FigJam, Dovetail, and Maze.</p>

          <p class="reveal">Figma is the contract. Not the deliverable — the contract between design, engineering, and product. When the dev opens a file and finds nothing surprising, I've done my job.</p>

          <p class="reveal">Shipped isn't done. Fullstory, Mixpanel, and Looker are how I find out if I was right. Most of the time I wasn't, not entirely. That's the loop.</p>

          <p class="reveal">The rest is leverage. Claude and Gemini compress hours of writing and reviewing into minutes. Raycast and Wisprflow strip friction from the parts of the day that aren't design.</p>

          <p class="reveal">The tools change. The habit doesn't. Five years ago this list had Sketch, Principle, and InVision. In five years it'll have things that don't exist yet. What stays: small problems, small answers, motion early, ship, measure, repeat.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="how-i-work-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

          <dl class="tool-index reveal">
          <dt>Research</dt><dd>FigJam · Maze · Dovetail</dd>
          <dt>Design</dt><dd>Figma · Jitter · Retune.dev</dd>
          <dt>Measure</dt><dd>Fullstory · Mixpanel · Looker</dd>
          <dt>Team</dt><dd>Slack · Loom · Linear · Notion</dd>
          <dt>Daily</dt><dd>Raycast · Wisprflow · Claude · Gemini</dd>
          <dt>Key hardware</dt><dd>Steelcase Leap v2 · Odyssey G9 · Logitech MX combo · Deltahub Carpio</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>

</Base>
